Add DryRun support for backup and restore (issue #448): a new spec.dryRun field on Backup, Restore and Schedule resources runs the full backup/restore workflow (item collection, filters, plugin actions, resource list) without any side effects — no backup tarball is created/uploaded, no resources are created/patched in the cluster, and no snapshots, PodVolumeBackups/PodVolumeRestores, DataUploads or DataDownloads are created. Logs, results and the backup/restore resource list are uploaded as usual; skipped items are marked as "dryrun" in the restore resource list. A --dry-run flag is added to "velero backup create" and "velero restore create" (note: the CR is still created and processed by the Velero server, unlike kubectl --dry-run). Plugins should check spec.dryRun before directly creating anything in-cluster.
